    LLM: 'Game: Whist Israeli. Exact-bid trick-taking; contract then trick bids; follow suit; highest trump or led-suit wins trick.',
    Player: 'Four-player exact-bid trick-taking; two-phase bidding, then play 13 tricks; score by exact bid.',
    objective: 'Each player aims to take exactly the number of tricks they bid in the second phase. Score 10 plus the square of tricks for exact bid; lose 10 per trick over or under. Zero bid has special scoring. First to reach agreed target score wins.',
    gameplay: "Two-phase bidding: first phase (dealer starts, clockwise) bids 5-13 tricks plus suit or no trumps (Bridge order: no trumps highest, then spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). After four consecutive passes, last bidder is declarer and trump is set. Second phase: other three players (declarer's left clockwise) each bid number of tricks (0+); fourth player cannot bid so total equals 13. Game is over if total>13, under if <13. Declarer leads; must follow suit; highest trump wins trick else highest of led suit. Winner of trick leads next. After 13 tricks, score each player.",
